<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Finnish Socialist Workers' Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Helsinki</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Red Finland, the revolutionary government that held southern Finland during the civil war of 1918 before its defeat by the Whites and Germany.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tensions after independence erupted into civil war in January 1918. On 28 January the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-finland">Red Guards</a> seized Helsinki, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-peoples-delegation">Finnish People's Delegation</a>, chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kullervo-manner">Kullervo Manner</a>, took power in the industrial south. In late February it was proclaimed the Finnish Socialist Workers' Republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Reds controlled the cities and industrial centres of southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a>, including Helsinki, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampere">Tampere</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turku">Turku</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyborg">Viipuri</a>. Their draft constitution mixed socialist ideas with parliamentary democracy, and they received arms from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>. Both sides committed terror, and the Red administration struggled with food shortages and military weakness.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The White army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-gustaf-emil-mannerheim">Mannerheim</a> won the decisive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tampere">Battle of Tampere</a> in April 1918, while German troops took Helsinki. Red <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a> collapsed in May, and about 80,000 Reds were held in prison camps, where some 12,000 died. Its leaders fled to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> and founded the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/finnish-socialist-workers-republic.jpg" alt="Finnish Socialist Workers' Republic" width="320" height="399"><figcaption>Image: Original map of the War: Ville Virrankoski. Base map of Finland in 1918: Jniemenmaa · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FinnishCivilWarMapBegin.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Helsinki</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kullervo Manner</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Finnish, Swedish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/finland">Finland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Red Finland, Suomen sosialistinen työväentasavalta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=finnish-socialist-workers-republic" aria-label="Finnish Socialist Workers' Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5201 163 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Finnish Socialist Workers' Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5521 419L5521 419"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 419h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5521 419h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5521 419h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Helsinki. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=finnish-socialist-workers-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

